Feature: slice-4 / admin-auth-guard (+ admin-shell-nav, shipped together)
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-4
Verified: 2026-05-28
Anchored to: docs/18 §7 (single-role RBAC) + §8.2 (admin console)

What was built
==============
- /admin route + layout that wraps every admin page in a single
  client component, `<AdminGuardAndShell>`, which handles both auth
  gating AND the chrome (sidebar + header). The two responsibilities
  are combined intentionally — Next.js refuses to serialise function
  children from server→client, so the guard can't inject the User
  into a separate shell via render-prop. The combined client wrapper
  is the simplest reliable shape.

- src/components/admin/AdminGuard.tsx → AdminGuardAndShell. Four
  states drive the render:
    loading      → centered "Sprawdzanie uprawnień…" status.
    signed-out   → forbidden card prompting login. CTA →
                   https://app.superwizor.ai/login (cross-origin,
                   §5 R3). NO redirect-bounce; we keep the user on
                   the page they tried to access and let them click
                   through.
    forbidden    → forbidden card with "back to home" CTA. Used
                   for both "GetMyProfile failed" and "role !=
                   SUPERWIZOR_ADMIN".
    allowed      → <AdminShell> + children.
  Role check uses identityClient.getMyProfile (empty request →
  backend resolves the caller from the bearer token). Accepts both
  numeric UserRole.SUPERWIZOR_ADMIN and the string proto-name
  "USER_ROLE_SUPERWIZOR_ADMIN" because Connect-Web JSON wire format
  defaults to enum names (same forward-compat trick as the Slice 3
  Playwright tests).

- src/components/admin/AdminShell.tsx — chrome. Left sidebar with
  brand mark + four nav items (Dashboard / Orgs / Users / Audit log).
  Active item highlighted with Ember/15 fill + frost text via
  pathname-based aria-current. Right side has a header with email +
  Sign-out button that calls auth.signOut() then redirects to the
  locale landing. Sidebar collapses to a top bar at md breakpoint
  (cosmetic refinement lands in Slice 6 polish).

- src/app/[locale]/admin/layout.tsx — server-component shell:
  setRequestLocale, generateMetadata (title from i18n key), then
  hands children to the client guard. Pre-renders both /pl/admin
  and /en/admin as SSG (the auth status hydrates on the client
  after first paint).

- src/app/[locale]/admin/page.tsx — Dashboard placeholder. Three
  cards linking to orgs/users/audit. firstName pulled from
  auth.user.displayName as a personalised greeting. Real dashboard
  widgets (live orgs count, sessions/day chart, recent audit
  events) land alongside features 3-8 when the AdminListOrgs +
  ListAuditEvents RPCs are exercised.

- i18n: messages/{pl,en}.json grow with `admin` namespace
  (metaTitle, loading, signin/forbidden copy, sidebar labels,
  header buttons, home dashboard cards).

How verified
============
1. `pnpm build` exit 0. Route table now includes:
     /[locale]/admin    ● SSG (×2 locales)

2. HTTP smoke:
     /admin    → 200
     /en/admin → 200

3. Puppeteer screenshots — guard's "signed-out" branch
   (puppeteer runs anonymous in this session, so the AdminGuard
   short-circuits to the "must sign in" forbidden card after the
   AuthProvider mounts):
     signin-required-pl-full.png: "Musisz się zalogować, aby
       uzyskać dostęp do panelu administracyjnego." + Ember
       "ZALOGUJ SIĘ" button → app.superwizor.ai/login. Centered
       glass panel.
     signin-required-en-full.png: English variant.

4. preview_console_logs(error) returns "No console logs". The
   AdminGuard's getMyProfile call would throw without a bearer
   token in a signed-in session; the catch sets status="forbidden"
   silently, no unhandled rejections.

Compliance with docs/18
=======================
- ✓ §7 single-role MVP: role check fetched server-side on every
  page load via GetMyProfile. No client-side Firebase custom
  claims trusted.
- ✓ §8.2 admin URL: /admin on the marketing origin (not
  app.superwizor.ai).
- ✓ §5 R3 origin discipline: sign-in CTA cross-origins to the app
  origin's /login. Marketing site never runs the Firebase login
  flow itself.
- ✓ §14.5: zero hard-coded UI strings; everything via
  useTranslations.

What the next sub-features build on top
=======================================
- feature 3 (admin-orgs-list): adds a /[locale]/admin/orgs route
  that fetches via AdminListOrganizations. The shell + guard
  already work; the orgs page is "just" the body content.
- features 4-8: similar — each lands a new admin route + reuses
  the shell + guard.

Known gaps (carried forward)
============================
- "Allowed" state not visually evidenced in this session (would
  need a signed-in SUPERWIZOR_ADMIN user — same constraint as
  Slice 3 features 1, 3-6). The Playwright pattern from Slice 3
  feature 8 is the path to evidence it: intercept GetMyProfile,
  return a User with role=SUPERWIZOR_ADMIN, assert the shell
  renders. That test can be added under tests/e2e/admin.spec.ts
  in a follow-up sub-feature.
- Mobile sidebar collapse to a top bar is sketched but not
  polished — Slice 6 i18n-polish-launch picks it up.

